bert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> Also seems like the state could be set in render directly\r\n\r\nTried and doesn't work since without the effect, when we update the errors internally with `setErrors(nextErrors)`, this will immediately set it back to the (now stale) `externalErrors` @atomiks \r\n\r\n> So this means we don't need to give them control of clearing errors\r\n\r\nYeah, useActionState reminded me of the redux-like flows that don't involve a lot of state, where you receive the \"next error state\" as a prop after doing the designated action (submit). Otherwise to use `errors` you must additionally create your own errors state plus remember to add `onClearErrors={setErrors}` which isn't really having control over the behavior anyway 😅 \r\n\r\nI think this would also be clearer with some more extensive documentation on server errors, probably in the form integration page?\r\n","created_at":"2025-11-06T04:20:29Z","updated_at":"2025-11-06T04:20:29Z","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/3136#discussion_r2497237785","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/3136","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/comments/2497237785"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/3136#discussion_r2497237785"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/3136"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/comments/2497237785/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":44,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":50,